{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"15 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,52.038,3.651,3.268,"Baazar Style Retail (Style Baazar)"],[13.889,14.731,51.365,2.373,2.124,"A Q2 loss, ₹175 cr more debt and a 325 MW solar plan"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Style Baazar runs 283 value-fashion stores in eastern India. Q2 FY27 results"],[13.889,22.289,52.966,1.809,1.634,"came on Saturday 14 Nov, after Friday’s close at a 52-week high. Revenue fell"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"10% to ₹478 cr as Durga Puja moved into Q3; that was known. The profit line"],[13.889,25.177,52.988,1.809,1.634,"was not: gross margin fell to 29.1% (30.5%), other expenses rose 21%, EBITDA"],[13.889,26.621,52.936,1.809,1.634,"fell 55% to ₹31 cr and the loss after tax was ₹32 cr, against a ₹51 cr profit that"],[13.889,28.065,52.962,1.809,1.634,"included a ₹41 cr one-off lease gain. H1 same-store sales fell 11.5%. Trailing"],[13.889,29.509,48.417,1.809,1.634,"twelve-month earnings are a ₹37 cr loss; the 73x P/E on data sites is stale."],[13.889,31.995,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Cash is the bigger issue. H1 operations used ₹151 cr (+₹109 cr a year ago) as"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"inventory rose ₹151 cr to ₹834 cr (143 days against 108) and other assets ₹132"],[13.889,34.883,52.936,1.809,1.634,"cr. Cupid has paid in ₹144 cr, of which ₹79 cr repaid loans (CARE), yet"],[13.889,36.328,52.962,1.809,1.634,"borrowings rose from ₹348 cr to ₹522 cr. We assume the pre-Puja stock"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"unwinds by March. On the same day the company gave two FY27 revenue"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"numbers (₹2,301 cr in the deck, ₹2,500 cr in its releases), targeted ₹5,600 cr and"],[13.889,40.684,52.931,1.809,1.634,"600 stores by FY29 and proposed a 325 MW solar plant. Its ₹30 cr saving and"],[13.889,42.128,52.934,1.809,1.634,"four-year payback imply ₹120 cr; at ₹4 cr per MW (our assumption) it costs"],[13.889,43.572,16.953,1.809,1.634,"₹1,300 cr, 2.3x net worth."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"We forecast Q3 revenue of ₹712 cr (+53%) with Puja and Diwali together, H2"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"growth of 38% (₹2,500 cr needs 65%) and FY27E net income near nil; the one"],[13.889,48.946,52.964,1.809,1.634,"broker on Yahoo has EPS of ₹8.9. For FY29E we have 479 stores, revenue of"],[13.889,50.39,52.934,1.809,1.634,"₹3,744 cr and EPS of ₹7.31. Our Dec-27 target of ₹205 is 33x (peer median)"],[13.889,51.834,52.951,1.809,1.634,"forward EPS of ₹6.22; the company’s ₹5,600 cr at our 1.7% margin gives ₹361,"],[13.889,53.278,52.962,1.809,1.634,"a cash-rent DCF ₹54. We rate the shares Underweight. Upside risk: a strong"],[13.889,54.722,52.951,1.809,1.634,"festive Q3. Also note promoter holding fell from 45.7% to 35.1% since March,"],[13.889,56.167,51.665,1.809,1.634,"six directors resigned since August and the company is suing Cupid for ₹28 cr."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,68.023,1.489,1.022,0.915,"200"],[15.268,65.409,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[15.268,62.807,1.489,1.022,0.915,"400"],[15.268,60.195,1.489,1.022,0.915,"500"],[17.147,68.717,5.656,1.022,0.915,"Nov 25Feb 26"],[24.303,68.717,3.123,1.022,0.915,"May 26"],[29.238,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Aug 26"],[17.427,69.888,5.665,1.275,1.111,"Style Baazar ("],[23.095,69.914,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[23.708,69.888,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[26.792,69.888,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.567,71.048,1.691,1.387,1.209,"IPO"],[25.867,71.048,1.103,1.387,1.209,"1y"],[30.279,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.998,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[15.277,72.114,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.372,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"18.5%"],[24.09,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"49.1%"],[28.808,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"32.5%"],[33.527,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"21.3%"],[15.492,73.179,1.476,1.387,1